{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1g81p1wep2xpVPVevCTay","type":"tool_result","content":"1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`materi\n1413:- `linger?: number`: Seconds the pieces lie around before they dissolve (default 4).\n1424:- `restore(b: Breakable): void`: Put a broken block back, whole (its old pieces dissolve as usual).\n1429:- `update(dt: number, standing = -1): void`: Per frame: tiles under `standing` (a collider handle: the character's `groundCollider`) start to shake, shaking tiles drop, dropped ones grow back; old chunks dissolve away.\n4948:const TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4951:Art pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n4956:type TransitionKind = 'fade' | 'iris' | 'diamonds' | 'dissolve' | 'dither' | 'blinds' | 'wipe' | 'curtain' | 'mosaic'\n3808:### interface SpringChainOptions\n3809-\n3810-- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n3811-- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n3812-- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n3813-- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n3814-- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n3815-- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n3816-\n4936:### interface TrailOptions\n4937-\n4938-- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939-- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940-- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941-- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942-- `tail?: number`\n4943-- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n2620:### spatialize()\n2621-\n2622-```ts\n2623-function spatialize(listener: Listener, at: V3Like, o: SpatialOptions = {}): Spatial\n2624-```\n2625-\n2626-Gain and pan of a sound at `at` for `listener`.\n2627-\n2628-### interface SpatialOptions\n3541:### analyzeClip()\n3542-\n3543-```ts\n3544-function analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n3545-```\n3546-\n3562:### interface ClipReport\n3563-\n3564-Objective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\n3565-are the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\n3566-velocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\n3567-real defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n3568-\n3569-- `name: string`\n3570-- `frames: number`\n3571-- `loop: boolean`\n3572-- `speed: number | null`\n2645:### interface VoiceSettings\n2646-\n2647-- `volume?: number`: 0..1 (default 1).\n2648-- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n2649-- `muffle?: number`: 0 (clear) .. 1 (behind a thick wall, under water): a low-pass filter closing down.\n2650-- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones.\n2651-\n2652-### type VolumeChannel","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69254de6-4061-470e-8e76-10f1ee96c6e5","uuid":"4007de48-dfc5-4637-9786-2e6b55a48108","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:56:56.216Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`materi\n1413:- `linger?: number`: Seconds the pieces lie around before they dissolve (default 4).\n1424:- `restore(b: Breakable): void`: Put a broken block back, whole (its old pieces dissolve as usual).\n1429:- `update(dt: number, standing = -1): void`: Per frame: tiles under `standing` (a collider handle: the character's `groundCollider`) start to shake, shaking tiles drop, dropped ones grow back; old chunks dissolve away.\n4948:const TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4951:Art pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n4956:type TransitionKind = 'fade' | 'iris' | 'diamonds' | 'dissolve' | 'dither' | 'blinds' | 'wipe' | 'curtain' | 'mosaic'\n3808:### interface SpringChainOptions\n3809-\n3810-- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n3811-- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n3812-- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n3813-- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n3814-- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n3815-- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n3816-\n4936:### interface TrailOptions\n4937-\n4938-- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939-- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940-- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941-- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942-- `tail?: number`\n4943-- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n2620:### spatialize()\n2621-\n2622-```ts\n2623-function spatialize(listener: Listener, at: V3Like, o: SpatialOptions = {}): Spatial\n2624-```\n2625-\n2626-Gain and pan of a sound at `at` for `listener`.\n2627-\n2628-### interface SpatialOptions\n3541:### analyzeClip()\n3542-\n3543-```ts\n3544-function analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n3545-```\n3546-\n3562:### interface ClipReport\n3563-\n3564-Objective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\n3565-are the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\n3566-velocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\n3567-real defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n3568-\n3569-- `name: string`\n3570-- `frames: number`\n3571-- `loop: boolean`\n3572-- `speed: number | null`\n2645:### interface VoiceSettings\n2646-\n2647-- `volume?: number`: 0..1 (default 1).\n2648-- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n2649-- `muffle?: number`: 0 (clear) .. 1 (behind a thick wall, under water): a low-pass filter closing down.\n2650-- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones.\n2651-\n2652-### type VolumeChannel","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A1g81p1wep2xpVPVevCTay","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
